, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": []}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=50%, source=both]\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Accelerated Phase:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, decreased circulating antibody level, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, bleeding easily\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Primary Myelofibrosis in Accelerated Phase:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Accelerated Phase:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, bleeding easily\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Primary Myelofibrosis in Accelerated Phase:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, ascites\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nChronic Myeloid Leukemia in Accelerated Phase vs Primary Myelofibrosis in Accelerated Phase:\n  Favours first:  abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, bleeding easily, blurred vision\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology, anorexia\n\nNOT typically seen in Primary Myelofibrosis in Accelerated Phase: autoimmune antibody positivity, hemophagocytosis\n\nRelated to Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: cd4+/cd56+ hematodermic neoplasm, hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, mast cell neoplasm\n\nRelated to Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, lymphoid leukemia (disease), lymphoma\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Accelerated Phase: chronic myelogenous leukemia, bcr-abl1 positive\n\nRelated to Primary Myelofibrosis in Accelerated Phase: acquired aplastic anemia, cellular phase chronic idiopathic myelofibrosis, familial myelofibrosis\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  and night sweats → pain → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts"}
